 1. Types of SQL Functions

SQL functions are mainly divided into:

A. Single-row / Scalar Functions


Work on one row at a time and return one result for each row.

Examples:

UPPER()
LOWER()
LENGTH()
ROUND()
COALESCE()


B. Aggregate Functions

Work on multiple rows and return one result.

Examples:

COUNT()
SUM()
AVG()
MIN()
MAX()